  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A HIGH output (1) results only if all the inputs to the AND gate are HIGH (1). If not all inputs to the AND gate are HIGH, LOW output results.</p><p>But in case of OR Gate, for&nbsp;the output to be 1, at least input one OR two must be 1.</p><p>NOR Gate&nbsp;reverses the logic state.</p><p>Therefore, for all possible combination of inputs, outputs at different stages will look like as given below.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/756664fc-32c5-4bba-8efa-0f8cca0ea65d-24694ff9-af60-4c3c-9855-076c0fd5d83e-9895008_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 157px;\" /></p>",
